WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.437
arXiv puts out thousands of papers a week. Nobody reads them all.

2
00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:10.537
Research Digest keeps the ones you care about, right on your own machine.

3
00:00:10.787 --> 00:00:13.261
Every result says why it ranked where it did.

4
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:18.789
Open one, and you get what it's about, and the closest papers you already have.

5
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:24.251
Or just ask. A model on this machine turns your question into the search.

6
00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:31.554
And your coding agent reads the same library, instead of the open web.

7
00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:35.223
Research Digest. Your library, not the internet.
